    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #329\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-124-mcp-integration-02-07-persist-mcp-tool-thr_baziju47de`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #124: persistence for MCP tool registrations and per-project grants, building on #123's `mcpServers` item-model foundation.\n\n- **Migration `0020_mcp_tool_registrations.sql`**: creates `mcp_tool_registrations` (server item id, tool name/schema/description snapshot, `active`, `requires_approval` default `true`, `risk_class` default `unclassified`, timestamps, unique `(mcp_server_item_id, tool_name)`) and `project_mcp_grants` (composite PK `(project_item_id, mcp_tool_registration_id)`, `granted` default `false`, FK to the registrations table).\n- **`mcp/mcpToolRegistrationsStore.ts`**: reads, a sync-facing `upsertMcpToolRegistration` (for the future tool-discovery issue #125) that preserves user-owned `risk_class`/`requires_approval` across re-syncs, and user-only mutations `setMcpToolRiskClass`/`setMcpToolRequiresApproval`.\n- **`mcp/mcpProjectGrantsStore.ts`**: reads and the user-only `setProjectMcpGrant` mutation. Neither table is wired into the item-model/proposal-confirmation machinery, so agents and proposal confirmation have no write path to grants.\n- Updated `testSupport/testDb.ts` truncate list and `index.ts` exports; added integration tests for defaults, uniqueness, re-sync field preservation, and grant idempotency.\n\nVerified: full backend suite (`pnpm run test` — unit, integration: 50 files/529 tests, e2e: 5 tests) passes with exit code 0, `tsc --noEmit` is clean, and `check:boundaries` (dependency-cruiser) reports no violations.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
